/P 165 0 R
/E (Gender-based violence remains a serious global issue that affects individuals and communities across the world. Despite significant progress in raising awareness and promoting equality, many people continue to face discrimination, violence and barriers to equal opportunities. Addressing these challenges requires not only effective national policies but also international cooperation, education and awareness.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (I encourage each of you to research your country's position thoroughly, understand the existing international frameworks concerning gender equality and the prevention of gender-based violence, and consider both the challenges and opportunities presented by different approaches. As you develop your solutions, remember the importance of protecting human rights, ensuring equal opportunities, supporting vulnerable communities, and addressing the social and structural factors that contribute to inequality. Most importantly, remember that Model United Nations is not simply about defending a position; it is about diplomacy, cooperation, and finding common ground.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
