265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 699 0 R
/E (Gender Equality: The ultimate human rights objective wherein all individuals, regardless of their gender identity or biological sex, possess equal rights, responsibilities, visibility, and opportunities. It implies that the systemic value placed on individuals and their access to societal resources must not depend on the sex they were assigned at birth.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 700 0 R
/E (Gender Equity: The operational pathway toward achieving equality. Equity recognizes that different genders have distinct needs, realities, and historical disadvantages. Therefore, it involves fairness of treatment, which may include identical treatment or treatment that is different but considered equivalent in terms of rights, benefits, obligations, and opportunities. Equal treatment in an unequal system does not yield fairness; equity balances the scale first.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
