323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 177 0 R
/T (Armed conflicts, political instability, and humanitarian crises drastically exacerbate pre-existing gender inequalities, exposing women, girls, and marginalized populations to heightened levels of violence. During times of war or crisis, formal state structures, judicial systems, and law enforcement mechanisms often collapse or become severely impaired. This breakdown of public infrastructure leaves civilian populations without baseline legal protection, enabling armed groups, military forces, and opportunists to commit human rights abuses with widespread impunity. In many conflict settings, sexual and gender-based violence is systematically utilized as a tactic of warfare to terrorize communities, assert control, and force mass displacement.)
/E (Armed conflicts, political instability, and humanitarian crises drastically exacerbate pre-existing gender inequalities, exposing women, girls, and marginalized populations to heightened levels of violence. During times of war or crisis, formal state structures, judicial systems, and law enforcement mechanisms often collapse or become severely impaired. This breakdown of public infrastructure leaves civilian populations without baseline legal protection, enabling armed groups, military forces, and opportunists to commit human rights abuses with widespread impunity. In many conflict settings, sexual and gender-based violence is systematically utilized as a tactic of warfare to terrorize communities, assert control, and force mass displacement.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 177 0 R
/T (Furthermore, forced displacement and emergency settings place refugees, internally displaced persons \(IDPs\), and asylum seekers in inherently precarious living conditions. Overcrowded refugee camps, informal settlements, and temporary shelters frequently lack essential security infrastructure, such as adequate lighting, private sanitation facilities, and safe community spaces. In these environments, economic devastation and the loss of traditional community support networks force many individuals into dangerous survival strategies, increasing their susceptibility to human trafficking, forced labor, exploitation, and child marriage.)
/E (Furthermore, forced displacement and emergency settings place refugees, internally displaced persons \(IDPs\), and asylum seekers in inherently precarious living conditions. Overcrowded refugee camps, informal settlements, and temporary shelters frequently lack essential security infrastructure, such as adequate lighting, private sanitation facilities, and safe community spaces. In these environments, economic devastation and the loss of traditional community support networks force many individuals into dangerous survival strategies, increasing their susceptibility to human trafficking, forced labor, exploitation, and child marriage.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 177 0 R
/T (The situation is further compounded by the severe disruption of essential services, including emergency healthcare, psychological assistance, and legal aid. Humanitarian organizations attempting to operate in crisis settings face physical danger, restricted access, and chronic underfunding, which significantly restricts their ability to provide life-saving interventions. Consequently, survivors in conflict zones face a dual crisis: an escalated threat of physical and sexual violence paired with a complete absence of the medical, psychological, and judicial resources necessary for recovery and justice.)
/E (The situation is further compounded by the severe disruption of essential services, including emergency healthcare, psychological assistance, and legal aid. Humanitarian organizations attempting to operate in crisis settings face physical danger, restricted access, and chronic underfunding, which significantly restricts their ability to provide life-saving interventions. Consequently, survivors in conflict zones face a dual crisis: an escalated threat of physical and sexual violence paired with a complete absence of the medical, psychological, and judicial resources necessary for recovery and justice.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
