/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (The Universal Declaration of Human Rights \(UDHR\) is a document adopted by the United Nations General Assembly that codifies some of the rights and freedoms of all human beings. Drafted by a United Nations \(UN\) committee chaired by Eleanor Roosevelt, it was accepted by the General Assembly as resolution 217 during its third session on 10 December 1948 at the Palais de Challiot in Paris, France. Of the 58 members of the UN at the time, 48 voted in favour, none against, eight abstained, and two did not vote.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2 443 0 R 4 444 0 R 6]
>>
