<<
/Title (9. United Nations Population Fund \(UNFPA\). Child Marriage.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1310 0 R
/Next 1306 0 R
>>
endobj
1309 0 obj
<<
/Title (Even where comprehensive legislation exists, the enforcement gap remains substantial due to weak institutional capacity and systemic corruption. Law enforcement and judicial institutions frequently suffer from underfunding, insufficient training on gender sensitivity, and prolonged trial procedures. These structural flaws result in exceptionally low conviction rates, which reinforce a public perception that judicial systems are indifferent to survivors. By failing to hold perpetrators accountable, state institutions inadvertently sustain a cycle of violence, undermining rule of law and signaling that human rights violations against marginalized groups carry little to no consequence.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1307 0 R
/Next 1311 0 R
>>
endobj
