1312 0 obj
<<
/Title (8. United Nations Population Fund \(UNFPA\). Gender-Based Violence.)
/Dest [35 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1314 0 R
/Next 1310 0 R
>>
endobj
1313 0 obj
<<
/Title (Armed conflicts, political instability, and humanitarian crises drastically exacerbate pre-existing gender inequalities, exposing women, girls, and marginalized populations to heightened levels of violence. During times of war or crisis, formal state structures, judicial systems, and law enforcement mechanisms often collapse or become severely impaired. This breakdown of public infrastructure leaves civilian populations without baseline legal protection, enabling armed groups, military forces, and opportunists to commit human rights abuses with widespread impunity. In many conflict settings, sexual and gender-based violence is systematically utilized as a tactic of warfare to terrorize communities, assert control, and force mass displacement.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1311 0 R
/Next 1315 0 R
>>
endobj
1314 0 obj
<<
/Title (10- BIBLIOGRAPHY)
/Dest [34 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1316 0 R
/Next 1312 0 R
>>
endobj
1315 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, forced displacement and emergency settings place refugees, internally displaced persons \(IDPs\), and asylum seekers in inherently precarious living conditions. Overcrowded refugee camps, informal settlements, and temporary shelters frequently lack essential security infrastructure, such as adequate lighting, private sanitation facilities, and safe community spaces. In these environments, economic devastation and the loss of traditional community support networks force many individuals into dangerous survival strategies, increasing their susceptibility to human trafficking, forced labor, exploitation, and child marriage.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1313 0 R
/Next 1317 0 R
>>
endobj
1316 0 obj
<<
/Title (11.How can stronger laws on gender-based violence pass into effect when, in many countries, prevailing social norms and institutions condone such violence against women?)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1318 0 R
/Next 1314 0 R
>>
endobj
1317 0 obj
<<
/Title (The situation is further compounded by the severe disruption of essential services, including emergency healthcare, psychological assistance, and legal aid. Humanitarian organizations attempting to operate in crisis settings face physical danger, restricted access, and chronic underfunding, which significantly restricts their ability to provide life-saving interventions. Consequently, survivors in conflict zones face a dual crisis: an escalated threat of physical and sexual violence paired with a complete absence of the medical, psychological, and judicial resources necessary for recovery and justice.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1315 0 R
/Next 1319 0 R
>>
endobj
