1323 0 obj
<<
/Title (This crisis within a crisis is further worsened by the widespread disruption of essential social support systems and legal protections. During widespread emergencies, resources and personnel from healthcare, social work, and law enforcement are frequently diverted toward primary crisis management. As a result, helplines, emergency shelters, and legal aid clinics experience significant operational capacity reductions or total shutdowns. The simultaneous restriction of physical movement and reduced access to digital communication tools prevent survivors from seeking emergency assistance or escaping abusive households.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1321 0 R
/Next 1325 0 R
>>
endobj
1324 0 obj
<<
/Title (7.What steps need to be taken to eradicate the worst forms of traditional practices which are perceived to be discriminatory to women and girl children, such as female genital mutilation \(FGM\), honor killings and dowry related violence?)
/Dest [33 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1326 0 R
/Next 1322 0 R
>>
endobj
1325 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ultimately, the Shadow Pandemic demonstrates that disaster response mechanisms often fail to incorporate gender-sensitive frameworks, leaving structural protection gaps during times of emergency. The compounded economic stress, job loss, and heightened psychological frustration during crises act as catalysts for perpetrator aggression, while leaving survivors with fewer economic means to leave. Addressing this phenomenon requires integrating gender-responsive policies into national emergency preparedness plans, ensuring that essential support services remain operational and accessible regardless of the crisis context.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
